# Aliro User Device boundary

Apply this rule when implementing or changing application behavior under
`applications/aliro-nfc-user-device/` or its functional tests. Investigation,
review, and harness/documentation-only maintenance do not require a target
unless they implement slice deliverables.

- An implementation request must explicitly provide
  `TARGET_SLICE=Cx.y`.
- If the target is missing, unknown, ambiguous, complete, or has an
  incomplete prerequisite, ask the user; never choose a slice.
- Execute exactly one slice from
  `applications/aliro-nfc-user-device/docs/harness/slices/` unless the user
  explicitly changes scope.
- Require the local, untracked `docs/Requirements.pdf` before interpreting a
  project requirement.
- Modify only application-owned code/tests in this repository.
- Never modify the sibling `ncs-aliro` checkout.
- Never duplicate, replace, patch around, or locally implement stack-owned
  protocol behavior.
- Record a precise stack blocker and stop that path when required behavior
  is missing or defective.
- Implementation leaves changes uncommitted.
- Commit only through an explicit verification/commit request after all
  selected-slice checks pass.
